title: "Allocating AI Compute for Global Educational Access"
type: report
authors:
  - name: "OpenAI Codex Research"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
version: "2.0.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22288883
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22288883"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/allocating-ai-translation-compute-for-educational-access"
abstract: >-
  Evidence-bound global research on allocating standardized new AI compute to
  exact written-language varieties and scripts, named sign languages,
  accessibility formats, and evidence-supported bridge designs in order to
  increase functional educational access. The release contains 1,077 authority
  targets, a 204-target direct-person comparison, two stage opportunities, a
  complete Top 100 reference order, sensitivity and partial-identification
  analyses, a multi-lane funding portfolio, stage-and-subject recommendations,
  and a reproducible accessible publication package.
keywords:
